 "final_summary": "The issue was that non-positive values from the environment (like -5) were being directly used as the default page size without falling back to the default value of 20. The fix modifies the `_coerce` function in `tracker/config.py` to reject non-positive integers and return the default value (20) instead. This ensures proper fallback behavior as required by the test, and all tests now pass.",
 "diff": "diff --git a/tracker/config.py b/tracker/config.py\nindex 9d02783..fb5bc1d 100644\n--- a/tracker/config.py\n+++ b/tracker/config.py\n@@ -41,6 +41,10 @@ def _coerce(name, value):\n             number = int(str(value).strip())\n         except (TypeError, ValueError):\n             return None\n+        # If the value is non-positive, fall back to the default\n+        if number <= 0:\n+            return DEFAULTS[name]\n+        return number\n         return number\n     if value is None:\n         return None\n",
